    "title":  "Overlap-stabilized orthogonal score estimator",
    "lifecycle_state":  "active",
    "scientific_question":  "Can a bounded overlap weight reduce finite-sample instability while preserving first-order orthogonality for an average treatment effect estimator?",
    "rationale":  "The method replaces inverse propensity weights with a smooth bounded weight inside an orthogonal estimating equation, targeting improved stability under limited covariate overlap.",
    "summary":  "Estimate the average treatment effect with a cross-fitted orthogonal score whose propensity component is smoothly bounded under weak overlap.",
